From 3f92d3ab211bc1ac00909c20fee20def0cccdbd6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sh1ftmaker <shiftmaker@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 21:43:11 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Bring shotzo.c, code_0806F734.c and sub_0800F044.c over
 from all-work

Upstream still has these three as assembly (asm/shotzo.s,
asm/code_0806F734.s, asm/sub_0800F044.s); the all-work branch had them
in C, with NAKED wrappers + NONMATCHING bodies for six functions
(sub_0811A934, sub_0811AA80, sub_0811AB74, sub_08098E54, sub_0809924C,
sub_0800F044) and their asm/nonmatching/*.inc.  Ported to current
upstream names: symbols by address against the current katam.elf,
struct Object/Object2/Object4 -> ObjectTemplate/Object/EffectObject,
Kirby's base.base.base -> base, ->object -> ->objTemplate,
ObjectBase/EffectObject unk0 -> header.kind.  make compare: OK.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
